          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "претензия (preténziya) is usually traced, probably through German, to Medieval Latin praetēnsiō 'a claim', from praetendere 'to stretch out, to put forward' (Lewis & Short). EtymDB does not list it, so the route is hedged."
